  "synthesis": {
    "description": "A desk coordinator records the origination recognized on deals each night, checks it against what was granted to each originating group, and follows up when amounts are missing from the schedule or a group claims more than it was granted. New groups are added to the origination file and given a daily report, and the coordinator asks who should grant origination on a given deal.",
    "steps": [
      "Origination recognized on the night's deals is totalled.",
      "The total is compared with what each originating group was granted.",
      "Missing or over-claimed amounts are raised with the group or the person granting origination.",
      "New groups' deals are added to the origination file and set up for a daily report.",
      "The schedule and report are corrected once the amounts are confirmed."
    ],
    "approach": "A template origination schedule that lists each deal, the group granted origination, the amount granted and the amount claimed or recognized, with a check column flagging differences and missing grants for follow-up.",
    "rationale": "The work is matching recognized and claimed origination against grants deal by deal; a shared schedule layout with a difference check makes gaps and over-claims visible without rebuilding the comparison each night.",
    "artifact_type": "template"
  },
  "formula": {
